.SH "TEXT FORMATTING"
.sp
.B Constrained (applied at word boundaries)
.br
\fBstrong importance\fP (aka bold)
.br
\fIstress emphasis\fP (aka italic)
.br
\f(CRmonospaced\fP (aka typewriter text)
.br
\(lqdouble\(rq and \(oqsingle\(cq typographic quotes
.br
passthrough text (substitutions disabled)
.br
\f(CRliteral text\fP (monospaced with substitutions disabled)
.br
a mark to remember (highlighted for notation)
.sp
.B Unconstrained (applied anywhere)
.br
\fBC\fPreate, \fBR\fPead, \fBU\fPpdate, and \fBD\fPelete (CRUD)
.br
fan\fIfreakin\fPtastic
.br
\f(CRmono\fPculture
.br
markup your text
.sp
.B Replacements
.br
